{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hpa4w95ATWFHh3ktqCgEHG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Burneo Dinarte-Diaz Lopez Molina \"Can EdTech Close Learning Gaps\" World Bank digital interventions meta-analysis\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"World Development Report 2026: Background Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldbank.org/en/publication/wdr2026/brief/world-development-report-2026-background-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Education Research from the Development Research Group\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldbank.org/en/research/brief/education-research-from-the-development-research-group\"},{\"title\":\"Research Initiatives\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/research/initiatives\"},{\"title\":\"EdTech in Developing Countries: A Review of the Evidence | The World Bank Research Observer | Oxford Academic\",\"url\":\"https://academic.oup.com/wbro/advance-article/doi/10.1093/wbro/lkab011/6333790\"},{\"title\":\"Computer-Based Intervention Closes Learning Gap in Maths Accumulated in Remote Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9397034/\"},{\"title\":\"EdTech Evidence Gaps - Education Technology\",\"url\":\"https://voxdev.org/voxdevlit/education-technology/edtech-evidence-gaps\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the paper you're looking for. \"Can EdTech Close Learning Gaps? Global Evidence from Digital Interventions\" is a paper by Alegria Burneo, Lelys Dinarte-Diaz, Carolina Lopez, and Ezequiel Molina. The paper is listed as a background paper for the World Bank Development Report 2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"d43c3c93-fa27-4691-8f18-033fb130c5cc","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:44:40.344Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Burneo Dinarte-Diaz Lopez Molina \"Can EdTech Close Learning Gaps\" World Bank digital interventions meta-analysis","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01A1pQarZP2UKp9REENtM8yi","content":[{"title":"World Development Report 2026: Background Papers","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/publication/wdr2026/brief/world-development-report-2026-background-papers"},{"title":"Education Research from the Development Research Group","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/research/brief/education-research-from-the-development-research-group"},{"title":"Research Initiatives","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/about/unit/unit-dec/research/initiatives"},{"title":"EdTech in Developing Countries: A Review of the Evidence | The World Bank Research Observer | Oxford Academic","url":"https://academic.oup.com/wbro/advance-article/doi/10.1093/wbro/lkab011/6333790"},{"title":"Computer-Based Intervention Closes Learning Gap in Maths Accumulated in Remote Learning","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9397034/"},{"title":"EdTech Evidence Gaps - Education Technology","url":"https://voxdev.org/voxdevlit/education-technology/edtech-evidence-gaps"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the paper you're looking for. \"Can EdTech Close Learning Gaps? Global Evidence from Digital Interventions\" is a paper by Alegria Burneo, Lelys Dinarte-Diaz, Carolina Lopez, and Ezequiel Molina. The paper is listed as a background paper for the World Bank Development Report 2026."],"durationSeconds":4.045299749999991,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0137iqGdd4HEUBDkFXaqJ3aR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"World Bank EdTech meta-analysis 14 RCTs \"191\" effect sizes 0.125 generative AI adaptive technology\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"LLAMA LIMA: A Living Meta-Analysis on the Effects of Generative AI on Learning Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.18685\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Transforming Learning or Empty Promise? A Meta-Analysis of Generative AI in Education\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/395891364_Transforming_Learning_or_Empty_Promise_A_Meta-Analysis_of_Generative_AI_in_Education\"},{\"title\":\"A meta-analysis of the effect of generative AI on productivity and learning in programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.04779\"},{\"title\":\"Can Generative AI Feedback Effectively Enhance Learning Outcomes? A Meta-Analysis of 36 Experimental and Quasi-Experimental Studies\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.3390/educsci16060816\"},{\"title\":\"Effects of GenAI Interventions on Student Academic Performance: A Meta-Analysis - Jiahe Gu, Zi Yan, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://doi.org/10.1177/07356331251349620\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring the impact of personalized and adaptive learning technologies on reading literacy: A global meta-analysis - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1747938X23000805\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI Mental Health Chatbots as Therapeutic Tools: Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Their Role in Reducing Mental Health Issues\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12707440/\"},{\"title\":\"The impact of GenAI on learning outcomes: A systematic review and meta-analysis of experimental studies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1747938X2500051X\"},{\"title\":\"Effects of Artificial Intelligence on Educational Functioning: A Review and Meta-Analysis | Educational Psychology Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10648-025-10085-5\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results on EdTech meta-analyses. The search results contain several meta-analyses on generative AI and adaptive technology in education, though the specific study parameters you mentioned (14 RCTs with 191 effect sizes and 0.125 effect size) don't appear to match any single study in these results.\n\nHowever, I did find one result that closely resembles what you're looking for: A meta-analysis of 14 RCTs showed a statistically significant effect (ES=0.30) on GenAI chatbots' effectiveness in reducing negative mental health issues, though this focuses on mental health rather than general learning outcomes and has an effect size of 0.30 rather than 0.125.\n\nThe search results also include several other relevant meta-analyses on AI and adaptive technology in education:\n\n- One meta-analysis yielded 337 effect sizes across various educational levels and revealed a moderate positive effect of GenAI on learning outcomes (SMD = 0.45)\n\n- Another comprehensive review examined 228 studies with 464 effect sizes, finding AI had large positive effects on cognition and psychological functioning, and moderate effects on knowledge utilization\n\n- Different types of AI had different effects on cognition, with generative AI demonstrating the largest effects compared to other types like intelligent tutoring and adaptive/personalized learning\n\nIf you're looking for a specific World Bank study with those exact parameters, it may not be in these search results, or the details may need to be refined.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"67dd6e18-44ab-4b5b-bfde-e07525fced94","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:44:43.484Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"World Bank EdTech meta-analysis 14 RCTs \"191\" effect sizes 0.125 generative AI adaptive technology","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BswJBDyHAnFxwG9CVvfCmc","content":[{"title":"LLAMA LIMA: A Living Meta-Analysis on the Effects of Generative AI on Learning Mathematics","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.18685"},{"title":"(PDF) Transforming Learning or Empty Promise? A Meta-Analysis of Generative AI in Education","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/395891364_Transforming_Learning_or_Empty_Promise_A_Meta-Analysis_of_Generative_AI_in_Education"},{"title":"A meta-analysis of the effect of generative AI on productivity and learning in programming","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.04779"},{"title":"Can Generative AI Feedback Effectively Enhance Learning Outcomes? A Meta-Analysis of 36 Experimental and Quasi-Experimental Studies","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/educsci16060816"},{"title":"Effects of GenAI Interventions on Student Academic Performance: A Meta-Analysis - Jiahe Gu, Zi Yan, 2025","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/07356331251349620"},{"title":"Exploring the impact of personalized and adaptive learning technologies on reading literacy: A global meta-analysis - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1747938X23000805"},{"title":"Generative AI Mental Health Chatbots as Therapeutic Tools: Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of Their Role in Reducing Mental Health Issues","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12707440/"},{"title":"The impact of GenAI on learning outcomes: A systematic review and meta-analysis of experimental studies - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1747938X2500051X"},{"title":"Effects of Artificial Intelligence on Educational Functioning: A Review and Meta-Analysis | Educational Psychology Review | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10648-025-10085-5"}]},"I found relevant search results on EdTech meta-analyses. The search results contain several meta-analyses on generative AI and adaptive technology in education, though the specific study parameters you mentioned (14 RCTs with 191 effect sizes and 0.125 effect size) don't appear to match any single study in these results.\n\nHowever, I did find one result that closely resembles what you're looking for: A meta-analysis of 14 RCTs showed a statistically significant effect (ES=0.30) on GenAI chatbots' effectiveness in reducing negative mental health issues, though this focuses on mental health rather than general learning outcomes and has an effect size of 0.30 rather than 0.125.\n\nThe search results also include several other relevant meta-analyses on AI and adaptive technology in education:\n\n- One meta-analysis yielded 337 effect sizes across various educational levels and revealed a moderate positive effect of GenAI on learning outcomes (SMD = 0.45)\n\n- Another comprehensive review examined 228 studies with 464 effect sizes, finding AI had large positive effects on cognition and psychological functioning, and moderate effects on knowledge utilization\n\n- Different types of AI had different effects on cognition, with generative AI demonstrating the largest effects compared to other types like intelligent tutoring and adaptive/personalized learning\n\nIf you're looking for a specific World Bank study with those exact parameters, it may not be in these search results, or the details may need to be refined."],"durationSeconds":6.626613125000003,"searchCount":1}}
