{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ScytVXxbmid1eyaEWro6f","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Kestin \"AI tutoring outperforms in-class active learning\" Scientific Reports 2025 Harvard physics effect size\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI tutoring outperforms in-class active learning: an RCT introducing a novel research-based design in an authentic educational setting | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97652-6\"},{\"title\":\"How Harvard Made Physical Sciences 2 Easy for Half the Class - AI Tutor Platform & VR Labs\",\"url\":\"https://www.victoryxr.com/how-harvard-made-physical-sciences-2-easy-for-half-the-class/\"},{\"title\":\"An AI tutor helped Harvard students learn more physics in less time\",\"url\":\"https://hechingerreport.org/proof-points-ai-tutor-harvard-physics/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutoring Outperforms Active Learning – A Major Study from Harvard\",\"url\":\"https://svch.io/ai-tutoring-outperforms-active-learning-a-major-study-from-harvard/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) AI tutoring outperforms in-class active learning: an RCT introducing a novel research-based design in an authentic educational setting\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/392839220_AI_tutoring_outperforms_in-class_active_learning_an_RCT_introducing_a_novel_research-based_design_in_an_authentic_educational_setting\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutoring Beats Active Learning in New Harvard Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.bookbotkids.com/updates/edtech/ai-tutoring-outperforms-classroom/\"},{\"title\":\"Review of Kestin et al.’s June 2025 Harvard Study on AI Tutoring | Educational Technology and Change Journal\",\"url\":\"https://etcjournal.com/2025/11/10/review-of-kestin-et-al-s-june-2025-harvard-study-on-ai-tutoring/\"},{\"title\":\"Agentic AI Ecosystems in Higher Education: A Perspective on AI Agents to Emerging Inclusive, Agentic Multi-Agent AI Framework for Learning, Teaching and Institutional Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.14266\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutoring Outperforms Active Learning | Research Square\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-4243877/v1)%C3%83%C2%A7al%C3%84%C2%B1%C3%85%C5%B8mas%C3%84%C2%B1ndan\"}]\n\nI found the study you're asking about. Here's what the search results show:\n\nKestin, Miller, Klales and colleagues published \"AI tutoring outperforms in-class active learning: an RCT introducing a novel research-based design in an authentic educational setting\" in Scientific Reports 15, 17458 (2025).\n\n**Study Details:**\nThe study took place in Harvard's Physical Sciences 2 course during the Fall 2023 semester, with roughly 180 students alternating between two conditions each week: one in-class guided by active-learning methods, and another at home using a purpose-built AI tutor.\n\n**Key Findings:**\nStudents learn significantly more in less time when using the AI tutor, compared with the in-class active learning. More specifically, students using the AI tutor achieved roughly twice the learning gains of those in the active-learning classroom. Additionally, on a test afterwards, students scored about 30% higher after using the AI tutor.\n\n**Effect Size:**\nWhile the search results report that students achieved \"twice the learning gains\" and scored \"about 30% higher,\" the specific formal effect size statistics from the paper are not fully detailed in these search results. To access the precise effect size measurements (such as Cohen's d), you would need to consult the full paper at https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-97652-6.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"80a364b2-07ac-4bbb-8f89-a444a87edee9","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:44:58.057Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Kestin \"AI tutoring outperforms in-class active learning\" Scient