{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fd9x4rSp1zCLv2e4hFPYhp","type":"tool_result","content":"# Study Details from Abstract\n\n**Full Abstract Quote:**\n\"This study evaluates the impact of a program leveraging large language models for virtual tutoring in secondary education in Nigeria. Using a randomized controlled trial, the program deployed Microsoft Copilot (powered by GPT-4) to support first-year senior secondary students in English language learning over six weeks. The intervention demonstrated a significant improvement of 0.31 standard deviation on an assessment that included English topics aligned with the Nigerian curriculum, knowledge of artificial intelligence and digital skills. The effect on English, the main outcome of interest, was of 0.23 standard deviations. Cost-effectiveness analysis revealed substantial learning gains, equating to 1.5 to 2 years of 'business-as-usual' schooling, situating the intervention among some of the most cost-effective programs to improve learning outcomes. An analysis of heterogeneous effects shows that while the program benefits students across the baseline ability distribution, the largest effects are for female students, and those with higher initial academic performance. The findings highlight that artificial intelligence-powered tutoring, when designed and used properly, can have transformative impacts in the education sector in low-resource settings.\"\n\n## Key Information Extracted:\n\n- **Number of students:** Not specified in abstract\n- **Duration:** \"six weeks\"\n- **Setting:** In-school (secondary education context)\n- **Composite effect size:** 0.31 standard deviations\n- **English effect size:** 0.23 standard deviations\n- **ITT/First-stage details:** Not provided in abstract"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"258b3318-ecbe-49d6-826e-b49a2b50bb14","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:45:56.650Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":61802,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Study Details from Abstract\n\n**Full Abstract Quote:**\n\"This study evaluates the impact of a program leveraging large language models for virtual tutoring in secondary education in Nigeria. Using a randomized controlled trial, the program deployed Microsoft Copilot (powered by GPT-4) to support first-year senior secondary students in English language learning over six weeks. The intervention demonstrated a significant improvement of 0.31 standard deviation on an assessment that included English topics aligned with the Nigerian curriculum, knowledge of artificial intelligence and digital skills. The effect on English, the main outcome of interest, was of 0.23 standard deviations. Cost-effectiveness analysis revealed substantial learning gains, equating to 1.5 to 2 years of 'business-as-usual' schooling, situating the intervention among some of the most cost-effective programs to improve learning outcomes. An analysis of heterogeneous effects shows that while the program benefits students across the baseline ability distribution, the largest effects are for female students, and those with higher initial academic performance. The findings highlight that artificial intelligence-powered tutoring, when designed and used properly, can have transformative impacts in the education sector in low-resource settings.\"\n\n## Key Information Extracted:\n\n- **Number of students:** Not specified in abstract\n- **Duration:** \"six weeks\"\n- **Setting:** In-school (secondary education context)\n- **Composite effect size:** 0.31 standard deviations\n- **English effect size:** 0.23 standard deviations\n- **ITT/First-stage details:** Not provided in abstract","durationMs":6642,"url":"https://ideas.repec.org/p/wbk/wbrwps/11125.html"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BGmfcRa9uSLXNwzZztGZd4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LearnLM \"Guided Learning\" Sierra Leone randomized trial mathematics 1763 students \"0.258\" OR \"0.26 standard deviations\" Gemini\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"LearnLM | Google Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/solutions/learnlm\"},{\"title\":\"Google Gemini Guided Learning raises math scores in Sierra Leone classroom trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.edtechinnovationhub.com/news/google-gemini-guided-learning-raises-math-scores-in-sierra-leone-classroom-trial\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini AI Boosts Math Skills in Sierra Leone Trial | StartupHub.ai\",\"url\":\"https://www.startuphub.ai/ai-news/ai-research/2026/gemini-ai-boosts-math-skills-in-sierra-leone-trial\"},{\"title\":\"Google and Fab AI Demonstrate AI’s Impact on Math Education - USBE and Information Technology\",\"url\":\"https://www.blackengineer.com/sample-section/ai-news/google-and-fab-ai-demonstrate-ai%E2%80%99s-impact-on-math-education/\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini’s guided learning: results from a randomized controlled trial in Sierra Leone\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/measuring-the-impact-of-learning-with-ai-in-sierra-leone-and-beyond/\"},{\"title\":\"Measuring the impact of Guided Learning on student ...\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_sierraleone_may26.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"9-6-2026 Teacher Training Materials for Junior Secondary Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_sierraleone_teacher_training_jun26.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"9-6-2026 Rapid Evidence for AI in Education: An RCT Playbook Sierra Leone\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_sierraleone_playbook_jun26.pdf\"}]\n\nPerfect! I found the information you were searching for. Here are the key findings from the LearnLM Guided Learning trial in Sierra Leone:\n\n## Study Overview\n\nThe preregistered trial involved 1,763 Grade 7 and Grade 8 students across 48 classrooms in 12 government-supported junior secondary schools in Port Loko District.\n\n## Key Results\n\nThe results, released in June 2026, showed an intent-to-treat effect of 0.258 standard deviations on math scores.\n\nEngaging with Gemini's Guided Learning mode for at least 12 hours over the 8-week trial significantly improved students' learning, giving them a large boost—equivalent to moving a student from the 50th to the 64th percentile in mathematics. By standard conversion, that gain reflects roughly 1.8 to 2.5 years of extra learning progress.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nTeachers in participating classrooms were asked to incorporate Gemini Guided Learning into two of their four weekly math periods, amounting to a target of 12 hours over eight weeks.\n\n## Pedagogical Approach\n\nGuided Learning is built from years of research and work in LearnLM efforts to be pedagogically-grounded and specifically tuned to prioritize building understanding over providing direct answers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"58fa2a7a-226a-4651-ae3e-8c4b48f4a1fc","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:45:58.842Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"LearnLM \"Guided Learning\" Sierra Leone randomized trial mathematics 1763 students \"0.258\" OR \"0.26 standard deviations\" Gemini","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015XZm31G3Ys8zBAKmrTNXp2","content":[{"title":"LearnLM | Google Cloud","url":"https://cloud.google.com/solutions/learnlm"},{"title":"Google Gemini Guided Learning raises math scores in Sierra Leone classroom trial","url":"https://www.edtechinnovationhub.com/news/google-gemini-guided-learning-raises-math-scores-in-sierra-leone-classroom-trial"},{"title":"Gemini AI Boosts Math Skills in Sierra Leone Trial | StartupHub.ai","url":"https://www.startuphub.ai/ai-news/ai-research/2026/gemini-ai-boosts-math-skills-in-sierra-leone-trial"},{"title":"Google and Fab AI Demonstrate AI’s Impact on Math Education - USBE and Information Technology","url":"https://www.blackengineer.com/sample-section/ai-news/google-and-fab-ai-demonstrate-ai%E2%80%99s-impact-on-math-education/"},{"title":"Gemini’s guided learning: results from a randomized controlled trial in Sierra Leone","url":"https://deepmind.google/blog/measuring-the-impact-of-learning-with-ai-in-sierra-leone-and-beyond/"},{"title":"Measuring the impact of Guided Learning on student ...","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_sierraleone_may26.pdf"},{"title":"9-6-2026 Teacher Training Materials for Junior Secondary Mathematics","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_sierraleone_teacher_training_jun26.pdf"},{"title":"9-6-2026 Rapid Evidence for AI in Education: An RCT Playbook Sierra Leone","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_sierraleone_playbook_jun26.pdf"}]},"Perfect! I found the information you were searching for. Here are the key findings from the LearnLM Guided Learning trial in Sierra Leone:\n\n## Study Overview\n\nThe preregistered trial involved 1,763 Grade 7 and Grade 8 students across 48 classrooms in 12 government-supported junior secondary schools in Port Loko District.\n\n## Key Results\n\nThe results, released in June 2026, showed an intent-to-treat effect of 0.258 standard deviations on math scores.\n\nEngaging with Gemini's Guided Learning mode for at least 12 hours over the 8-week trial significantly improved students' learning, giving them a large boost—equivalent to moving a student from the 50th to the 64th percentile in mathematics. By standard conversion, that gain reflects roughly 1.8 to 2.5 years of extra learning progress.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nTeachers in participating classrooms were asked to incorporate Gemini Guided Learning into two of their four weekly math periods, amounting to a target of 12 hours over eight weeks.\n\n## Pedagogical Approach\n\nGuided Learning is built from years of research and work in LearnLM efforts to be pedagogically-grounded and specifically tuned to prioritize building understanding over providing direct answers."],"durationSeconds":8.40669987499999,"searchCount":1}}
