{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RRbPormnG1YWjKe1Hsiaxe","type":"tool_result","content":"# Study Details from Sierra Leone RCT\n\n**Number of Students:** 1,763 junior secondary students\n\n**Number of Schools:** 12 schools in Port Loko District\n\n**Duration:** 8 weeks\n\n**Intent-to-Treat Effect Size:** +0.258 standard deviations in math scores\n\n**Treatment-on-Treated Estimate:** Students receiving approximately 12 hours of Gemini integration saw \"roughly 1.8 to 2.5 years of progress\"\n\n**Grade Levels:** Junior secondary (specific grades not detailed in the content)\n\n**Teacher-Led Format:** Yes, confirmed as a \"teacher-led intervention\" where \"Educators designed the lessons, set the objectives, and facilitated classroom discussions\"\n\n**Subject:** Mathematics\n\n---\n\n**Key Quote on Pedagogical Approach:**\n\n\"Gemini responded by posing scaffolding questions in 76% of its messages, providing direct solutions in only 2% of cases.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"75d2e995-303a-4488-b4b3-6491e13f1a3d","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:46:18.384Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":137369,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Study Details from Sierra Leone RCT\n\n**Number of Students:** 1,763 junior secondary students\n\n**Number of Schools:** 12 schools in Port Loko District\n\n**Duration:** 8 weeks\n\n**Intent-to-Treat Effect Size:** +0.258 standard deviations in math scores\n\n**Treatment-on-Treated Estimate:** Students receiving approximately 12 hours of Gemini integration saw \"roughly 1.8 to 2.5 years of progress\"\n\n**Grade Levels:** Junior secondary (specific grades not detailed in the content)\n\n**Teacher-Led Format:** Yes, confirmed as a \"teacher-led intervention\" where \"Educators designed the lessons, set the objectives, and facilitated classroom discussions\"\n\n**Subject:** Mathematics\n\n---\n\n**Key Quote on Pedagogical Approach:**\n\n\"Gemini responded by posing scaffolding questions in 76% of its messages, providing direct solutions in only 2% of cases.\"","durationMs":4721,"url":"https://deepmind.google/blog/measuring-the-impact-of-learning-with-ai-in-sierra-leone-and-beyond/"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NnjR33oPPzTMGyp1PMaFhf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"From Chalkboards to Chatbots\" Nigeria \"1,328\" students Copilot after-school\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Nigeria: World Bank Begins Education Programme On Generative Ai in Nigeria - allAfrica.com\",\"url\":\"https://allafrica.com/stories/202409300582.html\"},{\"title\":\"Artificial intelligence in English-language instruction: Looking at a pilot project from Nigeria\",\"url\":\"https://fordhaminstitute.org/ohio/commentary/artificial-intelligence-english-language-instruction-looking-pilot-project-nigeria\"},{\"title\":\"From chalkboards to chatbots: Transforming learning in Nigeria, one prompt at a time – Lifeboat News: The Blog\",\"url\":\"https://lifeboat.com/blog/2025/02/from-chalkboards-to-chatbots-transforming-learning-in-nigeria-one-prompt-at-a-time\"},{\"title\":\"Is two years of learning possible in six weeks with AI? – BOLD\",\"url\":\"https://boldscience.org/is-two-years-of-learning-possible-in-six-weeks-with-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutoring Breakthrough Delivers Two Years of Learning in Weeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.aifire.co/p/ai-tutoring-breakthrough-delivers-two-years-of-learning-in-weeks\"},{\"title\":\"From Chalkboards to Chatbots: Transforming Learning in Nigeria - Human Progress\",\"url\":\"https://humanprogress.org/from-chalkboards-to-chatbots-transforming-learning-in-nigeria/\"},{\"title\":\"From Chalkboards to Chatbots: How Generative AI is Reshaping Classroom Learning in Nigeria — AITrends.ng\",\"url\":\"https://www.aitrends.ng/post/from-chalkboards-to-chatbots-how-generative-ai-is-reshaping-classroom-learning\"},{\"title\":\"From chalkboards to chatbots in Nigeria: 7 lessons to pioneer generative AI for education\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/education/From-chalkboards-to-chatbots-in-Nigeria\"},{\"title\":\"From chalkboards to chatbots: Transforming learning in Nigeria, one prompt at a time\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/education/From-chalkboards-to-chatbots-Transforming-learning-in-Nigeria\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about the \"From Chalkboards to Chatbots\" initiative in Nigeria. However, I should note that the search results mention 800 students, not 1,328 students.\n\nOver June and July 2024, 800 first-year senior secondary students attended after-school English classes in computer labs twice a week. Each session began with the teacher introducing the week's topic, followed by students interacting with Microsoft Copilot, a generative AI tool powered by ChatGPT, to master the selected topics comprising both grammar and writing tasks.\n\nThe results of the randomized evaluation reveal overwhelmingly positive effects on learning outcomes. After the six-week intervention between June and July 2024, students took a pen-and-paper test to assess their performance in three key areas: English language—the primary focus of the pilot—AI knowledge, and digital skills. Students who were randomly assigned to participate in the program significantly outperformed their peers who were not in all areas, including English, which was the main goal of the program.\n\nThe initiative was conducted in Edo State, Nigeria, involving nine public secondary schools as part of a World Bank Education for Global Development initiative.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"4009e67e-1cdc-4048-bcfc-45e9752ed9b1","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:46:19.098Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"From Chalkboards to Chatbots\" Nigeria \"1,328\" students Copilot after-school","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Mof3DohsTd4FygALSBXwZp","content":[{"title":"Nigeria: World Bank Begins Education Programme On Generative Ai in Nigeria - allAfrica.com","url":"https://allafrica.com/stories/202409300582.html"},{"title":"Artificial intelligence in English-language instruction: Looking at a pilot project from Nigeria","url":"https://fordhaminstitute.org/ohio/commentary/artificial-intelligence-english-language-instruction-looking-pilot-project-nigeria"},{"title":"From chalkboards to chatbots: Transforming learning in Nigeria, one prompt at a time – Lifeboat News: The Blog","url":"https://lifeboat.com/blog/2025/02/from-chalkboards-to-chatbots-transforming-learning-in-nigeria-one-prompt-at-a-time"},{"title":"Is two years of learning possible in six weeks with AI? – BOLD","url":"https://boldscience.org/is-two-years-of-learning-possible-in-six-weeks-with-ai/"},{"title":"AI Tutoring Breakthrough Delivers Two Years of Learning in Weeks","url":"https://www.aifire.co/p/ai-tutoring-breakthrough-delivers-two-years-of-learning-in-weeks"},{"title":"From Chalkboards to Chatbots: Transforming Learning in Nigeria - Human Progress","url":"https://humanprogress.org/from-chalkboards-to-chatbots-transforming-learning-in-nigeria/"},{"title":"From Chalkboards to Chatbots: How Generative AI is Reshaping Classroom Learning in Nigeria — AITrends.ng","url":"https://www.aitrends.ng/post/from-chalkboards-to-chatbots-how-generative-ai-is-reshaping-classroom-learning"},{"title":"From chalkboards to chatbots in Nigeria: 7 lessons to pioneer generative AI for education","url":"https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/education/From-chalkboards-to-chatbots-in-Nigeria"},{"title":"From chalkboards to chatbots: Transforming learning in Nigeria, one prompt at a time","url":"https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/education/From-chalkboards-to-chatbots-Transforming-learning-in-Nigeria"}]},"Based on the web search results, I found relevant information about the \"From Chalkboards to Chatbots\" initiative in Nigeria. However, I should note that the search results mention 800 students, not 1,328 students.\n\nOver June and July 2024, 800 first-year senior secondary students attended after-school English classes in computer labs twice a week. Each session began with the teacher introducing the week's topic, followed by students interacting with Microsoft Copilot, a generative AI tool powered by ChatGPT, to master the selected topics comprising both grammar and writing tasks.\n\nThe results of the randomized evaluation reveal overwhelmingly positive effects on learning outcomes. After the six-week intervention between June and July 2024, students took a pen-and-paper test to assess their performance in three key areas: English language—the primary focus of the pilot—AI knowledge, and digital skills. Students who were randomly assigned to participate in the program significantly outperformed their peers who were not in all areas, including English, which was the main goal of the program.\n\nThe initiative was conducted in Edo State, Nigeria, involving nine public secondary schools as part of a World Bank Education for Global Development initiative."],"durationSeconds":4.738496041000006,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CnPmuzxayAYmdDrKdLyyKV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Muralidharan Singh Ganimian \"Disrupting Education\" Mindspark American Economic Review 2019 \"0.37\" math \"0.23\" Hindi 4.5 months\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India - American Economic Association\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257%2Faer.20171112\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India on JSTOR\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/26637210\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting education? Experimental evidence on technology-aided instruction in India - NYU Scholars\",\"url\":\"https://nyuscholars.nyu.edu/en/publications/disrupting-education-experimental-evidence-on-technology-aided-in\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India | NBER\",\"url\":\"https://www.nber.org/papers/w22923\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/aea/aecrev/v109y2019i4p1426-60.html\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22923/w22923.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"American Economic Review (Accepted September 2018)\",\"url\":\"https://econweb.ucsd.edu/~kamurali/papers/Working%20Papers/Disrupting%20Education%20(Current%20WP).pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting education? Experimental evidence on technology-aided instruction in India - Stockholm School of Economics\",\"url\":\"https://research.hhs.se/esploro/outputs/journalArticle/Disrupting-education-Experimental-evidence-on-technology-aided/991001480519906056\"},{\"title\":\"Disrupting Education? Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India | The Abdul Latif Jameel Poverty Action Lab\",\"url\":\"https://www.povertyactionlab.org/evaluation/disrupting-education-evidence-technology-aided-instruction-india\"}]\n\nPerfect! I found the paper you're searching for. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India\" is by Karthik Muralidharan, Abhijeet Singh and Alejandro J. Ganimian. It was published in volume 109, issue 4, pages 1426-60 of American Economic Review in April 2019.\n\nThe key findings you mentioned are all here: Lottery winners scored 0.37 sigma higher in math and 0.23 sigma higher in Hindi over just a 4.5-month period. \n\nThe study evaluated a computer-based adaptive learning platform (Mindspark) for secondary school students in urban India to measure the impact of customized learning technology on student test scores. The program increased test scores across all groups of students and was cost-effective compared to traditional schooling models.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d12dfc6-d7ef-4d13-8531-39e6848a761b","uuid":"6fa16c10-df85-4c67-b967-f30f4a45330f","timestamp":"2026-08-10T23:46:19.585Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Muralidharan Singh Ganimian \"Disrupting Education\" Mindspark American Economic Review 2019 \"0.37\" math \"0.23\" Hindi 4.5 months","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01WmYQgR44xhkWiwd7gpvA6J","content":[{"title":"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India - American Economic Association","url":"https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257%2Faer.20171112"},{"title":"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India on JSTOR","url":"https://www.jstor.org/stable/26637210"},{"title":"Disrupting education? Experimental evidence on technology-aided instruction in India - NYU Scholars","url":"https://nyuscholars.nyu.edu/en/publications/disrupting-education-experimental-evidence-on-technology-aided-in"},{"title":"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India | NBER","url":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w22923"},{"title":"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India","url":"https://ideas.repec.org/a/aea/aecrev/v109y2019i4p1426-60.html"},{"title":"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on ...","url":"https://www.nber.org/system/files/working_papers/w22923/w22923.pdf"},{"title":"American Economic Review (Accepted September 2018)","url":"https://econweb.ucsd.edu/~kamurali/papers/Working%20Papers/Disrupting%20Education%20(Current%20WP).pdf"},{"title":"Disrupting education? Experimental evidence on technology-aided instruction in India - Stockholm School of Economics","url":"https://research.hhs.se/esploro/outputs/journalArticle/Disrupting-education-Experimental-evidence-on-technology-aided/991001480519906056"},{"title":"Disrupting Education? Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India | The Abdul Latif Jameel Poverty Action Lab","url":"https://www.povertyactionlab.org/evaluation/disrupting-education-evidence-technology-aided-instruction-india"}]},"Perfect! I found the paper you're searching for. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n\"Disrupting Education? Experimental Evidence on Technology-Aided Instruction in India\" is by Karthik Muralidharan, Abhijeet Singh and Alejandro J. Ganimian. It was published in volume 109, issue 4, pages 1426-60 of American Economic Review in April 2019.\n\nThe key findings you mentioned are all here: Lottery winners scored 0.37 sigma higher in math and 0.23 sigma higher in Hindi over just a 4.5-month period. \n\nThe study evaluated a computer-based adaptive learning platform (Mindspark) for secondary school students in urban India to measure the impact of customized learning technology on student test scores. The program increased test scores across all groups of students and was cost-effective compared to traditional schooling 